<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Immae</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">272</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Immae was fought in 272 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> between the Roman emperor Aurelian and the army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palmyrene-empire">Palmyrene Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zabdas">Zabdas</a>. Aurelian's cavalry feigned flight until the heavily armoured Palmyrene horsemen were exhausted, then turned and defeated them. Aurelian then won again at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homs">Emesa</a>, besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palmyra">Palmyra</a> and captured Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zenobia">Zenobia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-immae.jpg" alt="Battle of Immae" width="320" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original:Demis project Current version:User:Barosaurus Lentus · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AurelianusPalmyra272.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
